import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 643 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 644 | 2026-10-24 | **Rhythm on the Home, part 3: group 5 'More rhythm' (Questions: time-signatures drill, level 9).** Counting kept as the app already has it from her earlier calls: 1 e + a for semiquavers, 1 trip let for triplets, 6/8 counted in quavers 1 2 3 4 5 6 grouped in threes with 1 and 4 strongest (Phase 464), 2/2 in minim beats (1 + 2 +). Lessons: Semiquavers (four on a beat; how many make a beat?), Triplets (three in one beat, a small 3 over the beam; two or three by ear), 6/8 time (six quavers, accented clicks on 1 and 4; how many quavers? which counts are strongest?), 2/2: cut time (the minim is the beat; which note gets one beat?), Syncopation (short-long-short, the long note on a +), Straight or swing? (the same quavers even or long-short; by ear). Engine: the rhythm chapter's renderer learns, all optional with the old defaults unchanged, a time signature's bottom number, triplets ('t3', with the 3), three quavers beamed in 6/8 ('e3'), and counts / hearts every countStep / heartStep with a countFn; the player and scorer learn a click unit (quavers in 6/8, minims in 2/2), accented clicks and swing. Also: 'Fill the bar' says 'the whole bar' for an empty bar (was '0 beats there already'). **Flag for her:** 당김음, 스트레이트/스윙, 2/2박자 '세로선이 그어진 C'; 'jazz and blues often swing'. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/{patch666.py,rq2.jsx,rq3.jsx}. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
